# pervej-shopify — track only what we author: docs, demos, tools, and each demo's theme/app
# code under shopify-dev/<id>/. Secrets, per-developer store config, Shopify CLI state,
# dependencies, builds and demo media never enter the repo. There is no database to leak:
# the stores live in Shopify's cloud, one per person. Change this file only on main (chore/ branch).

### Secrets & per-developer config ###
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Store domain and theme IDs differ per developer; the CLI gets them from tools/shopify/.env.local.
shopify.theme.toml

### Shopify CLI state ###
.shopify/

### Dependencies & builds ###
node_modules/
vendor/
# Function and extension build output is regenerated by the CLI.
/shopify-dev/*/app/extensions/*/dist/
/shopify-dev/*/app/extensions/*/generated/

### Logs and exports ###
*.log
# Theme zips downloaded from the admin: the theme is in git, the zip is noise.
*.zip

### IDE / OS / tooling ###
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
.claude/settings.local.json

### Upwork material never enters the repo (demo cycle runbook §1) ###
/upwork-feed*.md
/*picks*.md
/mining/

### Demo media never enters the repo (video guideline §4, §11) ###
/demos/*/media/
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4a
*.webm
